        {
          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "Interesting. The silhouette monotonically-ish increases toward 20, no clear elbow. This is a common problem — silhouette keeps rising because clusters fragment. Need a more robust approach: gap statistic? Or look at elbow of inertia, and stability analysis (consensus across seeds). Also note digits has 10 classes; ARI peaks around 10-20. The right answer: k=10 if we know ground truth, but purely unsupervised the metrics are ambiguous.\n\nLet me do:\n1. Elbow of inertia (kneedle-ish).\n2. Bootstrap stability: ARI between clusterings on subsamples/perturbations for each k → choose most stable.\n3. Silhouette per-k with confidence.\n\nAlso the raw (non-standardized) pixels might be better since standardization amplifies noise pixels. Let's compare: use PCA on raw /255 (no scaling) — standard practice for digits. Let me redo with unscaled data too, as a robustness check.\n\nLet me add stability analysis and elbow. Also maybe a \"gap statistic\" — expensive but doable with reference uniform data in PCA space.\n\nLet me write a second script.",
          "time": {
            "start": 1793526158921,
            "end": 1793526163410
          },
          "id": "prt_1967d5649001fk18FdKWFpGZ78",
          "sessionID": "ses_e698351c9ffetwbwn63Guk4V6d",
          "messageID": "msg_1967d53b9001Ujh2yAbH2otqJ7"
        },
        {
          "type": "tool",
          "tool": "write",
          "callID": "chatcmpl-tool-97dc61869e4791f1",
          "state": {
            "status": "completed",
            "input": {
              "content": "\"\"\"穩健性檢查：elbow、bootstrap 穩定度、以及不同前處理下的一致性。\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib\n\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom sklearn.datasets import load_digits\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.cluster import KMeans\nfrom sklearn.metrics import adjusted_rand_score, silhouette_score\n\nRNG = 42\ndigits = load_digits()\nX_raw, y = digits.data.astype(float), digits.target\n\nPREPS = {\n    \"raw/255 + PCA40\": lambda: PCA(n_components=40, random_state=RNG).fit_transform(X_raw / 255.0),\n    \"standardized + PCA40\": lambda: PCA(n_components=40, random_state=RNG).fit_transform(\n        StandardScaler().fit_transform(X_raw)\n    ),\n}\nks = list(range(2, 21))\n\n\ndef stability(Xp, k, n_boot=20, frac=0.8, seed=RNG):\n    \"\"\"子取樣重跑的 ARI 平均：越高代表該 k 的結構越穩定。\"\"\"\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    base = KMeans(n_clusters=k, n_init=10, random_state=seed).fit_predict(Xp)\n    scores = []\n    n = len(Xp)\n    for b in range(n_boot):\n        idx = rng.choice(n, size=int(n * frac), replace=False)\n        sub = Xp[idx]\n        lab = KMeans(n_clusters=k, n_init=10, random_state=seed + b).fit_predict(sub)\n        scores.append(adjusted_rand_score(base[idx], lab))\n    return float(np.mean(scores)), float(np.std(scores))\n\n\nresults = {}\nfor name, fn in PREPS.items():\n    Xp = fn()\n    inertia, sil, stab = [], [], []\n    for k in ks:\n        km = KMeans(n_clusters=k, n_init=10, random_state=RNG).fit(Xp)\n        inertia.append(km.inertia_)\n        sil.append(silhouette_score(Xp, km.labels_))\n        stab.append(stability(Xp, k)[0])\n    results[name] = dict(inertia=inertia, sil=sil, stab=stab)\n\n    # 相對慣性下降率（elbow）\n    drop = -np.diff(inertia) / inertia[:-1]\n    print(f\"\\n=== {name} ===\")\n    print(f\"{'k':>3} {'inertia':>9} {'rel_drop':>9} {'sil':>7} {'stability':>10}\")\n    for i, k in enumerate(ks):\n        d = drop[i - 1] if i > 0 else float(\"nan\")\n        print(f\"{k:>3} {inertia[i]:>9.0f} {d:>9.3f} {sil[i]:>7.3f} {stab[i]:>10.3f}\")\n    print(\n        f\"best sil k={ks[int(np.argmax(sil))]}, best stability k={ks[int(np.argmax(stab))]}\"\n    )\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(16, 4.2))\nfor ax, key, title in zip(\n    axes,\n    (\"inertia\", \"sil\", \"stab\"),\n    (\"Inertia (elbow)\", \"Silhouette\", \"Bootstrap stability (ARI)\"),\n):\n    for name, style in zip(results, (\"o-\", \"s--\")):\n        ax.plot(ks, results[name][key], style, label=name)\n    ax.axvline(10, color=\"gray\", ls=\":\", lw=1)\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"k\")\n    ax.set_title(title)\n    ax.legend(fontsize=8)\nfig.tight_layout()\nfig.savefig(\"figs/digits_k_robustness.png\", dpi=150)\nprint(\"\\nsaved figs/digits_k_robustness.png\")\n",
              "filePath": "/home/phonchi/.cache/oc-lab-redesign/runs/phase0/lab1-vague-4/project/cluster_digits_robust.py"
